6,Yurok Language Project: Yurok Song Recordings at Berkeley,https://linguistics.berkeley.edu/~yurok/web/songs.php,"W = T. T. Waterman Yurok field notebooks (University Archives CU 23-1, item 99) I. Ceremonial songs A. Brush Dance (with words or possibly with words) 1. Domingo of Weitchpec (1906, 1909): nine Brush Dance songs (H 809-813 [musical transcr. K], 1885-87, 1893) 2. Umits of Kepel (1906): Brush Dance song (H 876) 3.",Yurok,Algic
7,Home | Yurok Tribe,https://www.yuroktribe.org/,The Yurok Tribe is pleased to announce that we are able to offer our Amazon Business Prime account to all Yurok Tribal members. This new program allows you to take advantage of Amazon's wide product selection and competitive prices for business purchases. Shopping on Amazon Business is as user-friendly as Amazon.com. Additional benefits include: Free two-business day shipping with Business ...,Yurok,Algic
8,E5: Songs for Learning Yurok Part 1 - Yurok Language,https://www.yuroklanguage.com/yurok-in-20-podcast/e5-songs-for-learning-yurok-part-1,"Welcome to Episode 5 of the Yurok Tribe Language Program's ""Yurok in 20!"" Podcast! The purpose of this podcast is to provide a space for Yurok language learners to listen to elder audio, follow along with short lessons, practice speaking and listening to the Yurok language, and touch upon Yurok culture as it relates to what we are learning.",Yurok,Algic
9,Yurok | PLP,https://www.phoenixlanguageproject.org/yurok,"Yurok is an Algic language spoken in northwestern California in the United States. It is the native language of the Yurok tribe. The Yurok tribe was very prosperous before the arrival of European colonists, with nearly 50 villages established along the Klamath River and western coast of California. The proximity of the tribe to these water sources was crucial to the development of certain ...",Yurok,Algic
